      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-03-06T10:06:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I do enjoy the ambiguity of Ambuscade, it's true.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I'd have to go with \"The Rotting God,\" \"Setting Sun,\" \"Anthropoid,\" (with \"Crew, Viking\" a close second - there's just something about La Capitan which makes for amazing descriptors) and... an Environment card?&nbsp; \"Anomaly, Dinosaur\" is pretty amazing, but I also feel a draw towards \"The Last X,\" which I always feel adds a special degree of flavor.&nbsp; And, of course, \"Mummy, Trial\" has a tidiness about it, as well.</p>",
